{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Spec Steering Compliance Check",
  "description": "Before executing any spec task, remind the agent to read and follow the spec-workflow-automation.md steering rules, including the 5-round review process for each document phase.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "preTaskExecution"
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "MANDATORY: Before proceeding with this task, you MUST:\n1. Re-read .kiro/steering/spec-workflow-automation.md to refresh the workflow rules\n2. Identify which phase you are in (requirements/design/tasks/execution)\n3. If generating a document (requirements.md, design.md, tasks.md), you MUST perform the 5-round review process IN THE CHAT (not delegated to a subagent) so the user can see each round:\n   - Round 1: 完整性 (structure completeness)\n   - Round 2: 准确性 (accuracy, cross-document consistency)\n   - Round 3: 依赖 (dependencies, code-level verification)\n   - Round 4: 边界条件 (edge cases)\n   - Round 5: 矛盾 (contradictions)\n4. Each round MUST actually read code files using readCode/grepSearch/fileSearch\n5. Fix issues immediately, don't defer\n6. State \"第 N 轮未发现问题\" if no issues found in a round\nDO NOT skip or delegate the review process."
  }
}